From d5d14d3b66b6a9e32e2df7b10dc3e665c9a893b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:53:23 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] render: fold-free liquid glass lensing; drop the busy
 measure

Two artifacts: jagged polygons inside small glass over sharp edges, and
patches that slid around while glass animated.
- The busy-content measure (crisp vs frosted at 5 taps 24 px apart) is
  large only on edges, so it painted five shifted copies of every edge
  behind the glass. Removed until there is a blurred detail map.
- The strict Snell trace folds the backdrop into a mirror image near the
  rim; replaced by a fold-free squeeze, strongest at the rim
  (thickness*(ior-1), capped at 0.45*bevel), falling off as (1-x)^2; the
  light still uses the true squircle slope. Dispersion spreads that shift.
- Capture padded 28 px around the shapes (blur needs real backdrop there);
  the darkened outer edge is much fainter.
---
 src/render_helpers/liquid_glass.rs           | 10 ++-
 src/render_helpers/shaders/liquid_glass.frag | 82 +++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)

